Q: How to have a default DatePicker value in Filament 4? A: <p>The filters form is special here, <strong>ignoring default values from DatePickers</strong>.</p>
<p>You can however <strong>achieve your desired behavior by assigning to the Livewire component properties</strong> in the <a href="https://livewire.laravel.com/docs/3.x/lifecycle-hooks#mount" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>mount()</code> lifecycle hook method</a> (called when the Livewire component is created):</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>class Dashboard extends BaseDashboard
{
    use HasFiltersForm;

    ...

    public function mount(): void
    {
        // The default values here precede the ones in the Filament/Helper/DateHelper
        $this-&gt;filters['startDate'] ??= now()-&gt;startOfYear()-&gt;toDateString();
        $this-&gt;filters['endDate']   ??= now()-&gt;endOfYear()-&gt;toDateString();
    }
}
</code></pre>
<blockquote>
<p>Reminder: &quot;<a href="https://filamentphp.com/docs/4.x/getting-started#custom-pages" rel="nofollow noreferrer">every page class in a Filament panel is a Livewire component</a>&quot;.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The <code>??=</code> (null coalescing assignment operator) prevents overwriting the value if the user already selected a date.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Note: in the dashboard class that defines the page filters, the variable is called <code>$this-&gt;filters</code>. Only in the widgets classes that interact with it it's <code>$this-&gt;pageFilters</code>.</p>
</blockquote>
